  "captions": [
    {"start": 0.321, "end": 2.881, "lines": ["Outbreaks","of paralytic shellfish poisoning,"]},
    {"start": 2.881, "end": 8.161, "lines": ["or PSP, are specifically caused","by neurotoxins produced by a toxic,"]},
    {"start": 8.161, "end": 13.921, "lines": ["single-celled species of marine","algae known as Alexandrium catinella."]},
    {"start": 13.921, "end": 19.201, "lines": ["Shellfish like clams, mussels,","and crabs eat microscopic algae,"]},
    {"start": 19.201, "end": 21.121, "lines": ["including Alexandrium."]},
    {"start": 21.121, "end": 24.481, "lines": ["During a bloom of Alexandrium,","the concentrations"]},
    {"start": 24.481, "end": 29.2, "lines": ["of neurotoxins can reach dangerous levels","in the tissues of these shellfish,"]},
    {"start": 29.2, "end": 31.36, "lines": ["making them unsafe to eat."]},
    {"start": 31.36, "end": 35.44, "lines": ["In many indigenous communities","on the Alaskan coast, shellfish"]},
    {"start": 35.44, "end": 39.44, "lines": ["have traditionally made up a significant","portion of people's diets."]},
    {"start": 39.44, "end": 43.2, "lines": ["Canna is a tribal health","and social services organization"]},
    {"start": 43.2, "end": 47.92, "lines": ["serving Alaskan Native and American","Indian people in the Coniag region,"]},
    {"start": 47.92, "end": 51.6, "lines": ["with many services also available","to the wider community."]},
    {"start": 51.6, "end": 55.456, "lines": ["They have been working to monitor","and track PSP in the area."]},
    {"start": 55.456, "end": 59.376, "lines": ["Casey Joe Wright is an environmental","technician working with Canna."]},
    {"start": 59.376, "end": 64.096, "lines": ["We spoke to them near Kodiak Island","where they help monitor Alexandria."]},
    {"start": 64.096, "end": 67.376, "lines": ["So the native people of Kodiak,"]},
    {"start": 67.376, "end": 72.976, "lines": ["the Alutik-Sukpiak people, have lived","on this island for almost 10,000 years."]},
    {"start": 72.976, "end": 76.736, "lines": ["And so until now,","they have been able to rely"]},
    {"start": 76.736, "end": 79.936, "lines": ["on traditional knowledge","of when to harvest."]},
    {"start": 79.936, "end": 83.576, "lines": ["And those indigenous ways","of knowing are passed down."]},
    {"start": 83.84, "end": 87.84, "lines": ["Generation to generation and accumulated"]},
    {"start": 87.84, "end": 92.16, "lines": ["and really enhanced with each person."]},
    {"start": 92.16, "end": 95.68, "lines": ["Alexandrium, the organism that causes PSP,"]},
    {"start": 95.68, "end": 98.88, "lines": ["is extremely sensitive","to temperature changes."]},
    {"start": 98.88, "end": 101.84, "lines": ["It blooms historically","during summer months."]},
    {"start": 101.84, "end": 104.48, "lines": ["However, rising temperatures year-round"]},
    {"start": 104.48, "end": 109.68, "lines": ["have increased the likelihood","of PSP in the spring and fall as well."]},
    {"start": 109.68, "end": 113.648, "lines": ["There are people that Previously,","they have harvested their whole lives,"]},
    {"start": 113.648, "end": 117.648, "lines": ["who grew up harvesting,","and now are in their later years"]},
    {"start": 117.648, "end": 123.008, "lines": ["and won't do it anymore","because of this fear of it."]},
    {"start": 123.008, "end": 124.128, "lines": ["Because it's"]},
    {"start": 124.128, "end": 130.688, "lines": ["the toxin is showing up earlier","in the spring and later in the fall."]},
    {"start": 130.688, "end": 134.528, "lines": ["And whereas this was a more"]},
    {"start": 134.528, "end": 140.168, "lines": ["wintertime source of subsistence","for the communities on our island."]},
    {"start": 141.056, "end": 146.536, "lines": ["It also in the colder months","of spring and fall, people were not…"]},
    {"start": 147.456, "end": 150.656, "lines": ["expecting based on years"]},
    {"start": 150.656, "end": 154.016, "lines": ["of traditional knowledge","for it to show up."]},
    {"start": 154.016, "end": 159.456, "lines": ["So, our goal is not to replace","this traditional knowledge,"]},
    {"start": 159.456, "end": 165.536, "lines": ["but to adapt","with it to a change of ecosystem"]},
    {"start": 165.536, "end": 169.496, "lines": ["and support the gaps where we can."]},
    {"start": 169.968, "end": 172.208, "lines": ["Intertwined with the cultural tradition"]},
    {"start": 172.208, "end": 176.048, "lines": ["of shellfish harvesting is the role","that shellfish harvesting plays"]},
    {"start": 176.048, "end": 180.368, "lines": ["in providing a degree of economic","independence for some communities."]},
    {"start": 180.368, "end": 187.248, "lines": ["It's a difficult process to get food","and groceries out to the villages."]},
    {"start": 187.248, "end": 190.208, "lines": ["They don't always have like their pick","of what's available"]},
    {"start": 190.208, "end": 193.608, "lines": ["and there may be surcharges for…"]},
    {"start": 195.168, "end": 199.824, "lines": ["the extra distance that is gone","or Supplies needed immediately"]},
    {"start": 199.824, "end": 203.664, "lines": ["might have to be flown out and paid","with extra fees."]},
    {"start": 203.664, "end": 209.624, "lines": ["So there's the economic resilience","of these communities."]}
  ]
